o trek over to the main post office on Loyola. Do a good job at packing and shipping. Nice selection of cards and other touristy trinkets. Dog friendly!"},{"business_id":"QlgkDPk0aS19t8L4aKT2zw","review_id":"u_XOHyLnFZ1SP3fVoAGm0A","date":"2015-08-18T19:41:57","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.8981288075447083,"text_excerpt":"This place is easily the most charming and least depressing post office I've ever seen. If you're visiting NOLA, grab a postcard from the voodoo shop nearby and stop in here to send the folks back home some local flavor. If you live here, this is the best place to handle your postal needs. Yes, it's on Bourbon, but the nightly circus doesn't really kick in until after office hours. Plus, postal clerks actually smile here!"},{"business_id":"QlgkDPk0aS19t8L4aKT2zw","review_id":"0MOVTK8ZUxP3GdRA9yikXQ","date":"2014-04-03T16:05:04","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.8877154588699341,"text_excerpt":"This is great place to get some unique gifts and to send a package if you must. The staff was very friendly when I requested some information."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
